# Manual editor snapshots of the paper and thesis sources.
*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded MOS artefacts. Kept on disk as the local audit trail, untracked so
# the public release ships one authoritative file per result rather than the
# collection history beside it.
#   pilot/result_1..7.csv  incremental Qualtrics exports during collection. Every
#     response in them is also in N40.csv, which is the closed N=40 dataset and
#     the one every analysis reads. result_1.csv additionally holds nine columns
#     that exist nowhere else (the *_RATE3 AI-rerank ratings retired on
#     2026-08-07, the pre-split consent fields, two flow-order fields), which is
#     why these are ignored rather than deleted.
#   ab_results_n3.json     the n=3 Part 2 pilot, superseded by ab_results.json.
#   power_simulation_ALLSETS_superseded.json  named superseded; PROJECT_STATE.md
#     cites it for comparison and that file does not ship either.
results/mos/pilot/result_*.csv
results/mos/session2/ab_results_n3.json
results/mos/power_simulation_ALLSETS_superseded.json

# The pre-AI-removal Qualtrics tables. Kept on disk, untracked: they are only the INPUT
# that produced results/mos/qualtrics/loopmap_block<N>.csv, and it is those loopmaps that
# qualtrics_to_responses.py reads. The loopmaps ship, so the analysis path is unaffected;
# what a release loses is the ability to regenerate them with make_loop_index_map.py.
results/mos/qualtrics/archive_2026-08-07_pre_ai_removal/

# Presentation and pilot scaffolding. Kept on disk, untracked: none of it is an input to
# a reported number. cocola_pilot is the author-rated self-pilot, which the thesis uses
# only to place the |dC| ~ 0.025 audibility floor and never as evidence of preference, so
# the floor is stated in the prose and the raw pilot does not need to ship. demo/ is a
# walkthrough page built from that pilot, and level_review/ is the loudness-matching
# review UI whose chosen levels are already baked into the rendered stimuli.
results/mos/demo/
results/mos/level_review/
results/mos/cocola_pilot/

# The MuseCPEval comparison (arXiv 2512.14629v2, ISMIR 2026) was held back while the
# paper did not report it. The paper now reports it in Tables 3 and 4 and Section 5.1, so
# scripts/analysis/{diagnose,musecp_*}.py, results/musecp/ and
# results/diagnostics/diagnosis_musecp.json are tracked and ship with the release.

# Style-reference corpus. Kept on disk, untracked: 32 MB of third-party arXiv PDFs and
# LaTeX sources for the 13 accepted ICASSP papers behind doc/notes/icassp_house_style_
# 2026-08-25.md. They are someone else's copyrighted work, they are re-fetchable from the
# arXiv ids in icassp_examples/ids.txt, and nothing in the repo reads them.
doc/paper/icassp_examples/

# The official ICASSP 2027 template kit, downloaded 2026-09-04. Kept on disk, untracked:
# it is the conference's own distribution and re-fetchable from the URLs in
# doc/paper/README.md. The two files the draft actually compiles against, spconf.sty and
# IEEEbib.bst, sit in doc/paper/ and are NOT covered by this rule.
doc/paper/icassp_kit/
